// agentgateway-native: reject an incomplete FLAT tool result (mcpGuardrails, response phase)
//
// For tools whose structuredContent is the record itself (not a `results` list), e.g.
// rci-knowledge `lookup_opps`. Same threshold as block_incomplete_result.cel:
// completeness < 0.4, where completeness = fraction of REQUIRED fields that are
// present and non-null.
//
// EDIT: the tool name and the REQUIRED list. Scope the rule to one tool with the
// `mcp.tool.name ==` guard; without it the rule would run on every tool's result.
//
// Real example (rci-knowledge, 2026-11-06): lookup_opps for CPT 99213 returns
// status_indicator "B" and null payment_rate, relative_weight and all copayment
// fields, so a caller that needs a payment gets 0 of 5 payment fields and this
// rule rejects it. CPT 71046 has payment data and passes.

mcp.tool.name == "lookup_opps" &&
has(mcp.result.structuredContent) &&
mcp.result.structuredContent.with(r,
  ["payment_rate", "relative_weight", "national_unadjusted_copayment",
   "minimum_unadjusted_copayment", "adjusted_copayment"].with(req,
    double(size(req.filter(k, k in r && r[k] != null))) / double(size(req)) < 0.4))
